Hi

I am unsure about this term (and the similar ones with S...2 and S...3,

	f(Year, Scenario1, model= "rw2")

is this what you want ? I guess Scienario1 is binary with 1 at no 1, and
zero otherwise ??

if you think the trend is similar but different, then you might do

f(Year, model="rw2", scale.model=TRUE, replicate=Scenario)

where 'Scenario' is either 1, 2 or 3. This gives three ((prior)
conditional independent) trends with the same amount of smoothing.

if you think they are similar but correlated, you might do

f(Year, model="rw2", scale.model=TRUE, group=Scenario)

If you think the trends are the same, then

	f(Year, model="rw2", scale.model=TRUE)

will do

let me know.

Best
H

